---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import { getCaseStudy } from '../../data/caseStudies';

const cs = getCaseStudy('yungprime');

const metaTitle = 'YUNGPRIME Case Study: +28% Organic Sales | Share It Studio';
const description =
  'How a unified Amazon content strategy for slip-resistant work shoes grew YUNGPRIME’s organic sales by 28.3% and ROAS to 2.81× while ad spend went down.';

const results = [
  { metric: 'Organic sales', before: '$16,432', after: '$21,077', change: '+28.3%', highlight: true },
  { metric: 'ROAS', before: '2.63×', after: '2.81×', change: '+6.8%' },
  { metric: 'Ads CVR', before: '3.46%', after: '3.88%', change: '+0.42 pts' },
  { metric: 'Organic CVR', before: '2.74%', after: '2.96%', change: '+0.22 pts' },
];
---

<ArticleLayout
  kind="case-study"
  caseStudy={cs}
  title="How YUNGPRIME grew organic Amazon sales by 28.3% in one month"
  highlight="28.3% in one month"
  lead="A unified listing, A+ Content, Brand Story, Storefront and video for slip-resistant work shoes — more organic sales and a higher ROAS, with less ad spend."
  metaTitle={metaTitle}
  description={description}
  tags={['May – Jun 2026']}
  service={{ label: 'Amazon Listing Optimization', href: '/services/amazon-listing-optimization' }}
>
  <div class="article-body">
    <aside>
      <p>
        <strong>In short:</strong> YUNGPRIME’s listing, A+ Content, Brand Story and Storefront lacked consistency and
        clear differentiation. We rebuilt them around buyer research. From May to June 2026,{' '}
        <strong>organic sales grew +28.3%</strong>, <strong>total sales +14.1%</strong> and{' '}
        <strong>ROAS rose to 2.81×</strong> — while ad spend went down 2.85%.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <section id="client-background">
      <h2>Client Background</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>YUNGPRIME</strong> is an Amazon footwear brand specializing in{' '}
        <strong>slip-resistant work shoes</strong> for professionals, including healthcare and food service workers.
        With a competitive product and strong customer reviews, the brand had an opportunity to grow sales through more
        effective Amazon content.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="initial-challenge">
      <h2>Initial Challenge</h2>
      <p>
        Despite a strong product, YUNGPRIME’s <strong>Amazon listing, A+ Content, Brand Story and Storefront</strong>{' '}
        lacked consistency and clear product differentiation.
      </p>
      <p>
        The brand needed to communicate its benefits more effectively, address customer objections, improve conversions
        and <strong>reduce its reliance on paid advertising</strong>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="our-approach">
      <h2>Our Approach</h2>
      <p>
        We developed a research-driven Amazon content strategy focused on a consistent shopping experience across every
        touchpoint.
      </p>
      <p>
        By analyzing competitors, customer reviews, purchasing concerns and product positioning, we set a{' '}
        <strong>content hierarchy</strong> designed to guide shoppers from product discovery to purchase.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="implementation">
      <h2>Implementation</h2>
      <ol class="steps-list">
        <li>
          <h3>Market research</h3>
          <p>Analyzed competitor listings, customer reviews, objections and purchasing concerns.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Listing optimization</h3>
          <p>
            Redesigned the main images, infographics and image sequence around product benefits and buyer questions.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>A+ Content</h3>
          <p>Created structured modules that highlight product advantages, address objections and build trust.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Brand Story & Storefront</h3>
          <p>Developed consistent brand messaging and organized the shopping experience around customer needs.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Copywriting</h3>
          <p>Optimized product titles and bullet points to emphasize relevant benefits and product differentiation.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Product video</h3>
          <p>Created demonstration content showing product features and real-world use.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="results">
      <h2>Results</h2>
      <p>May vs. June 2026:</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Metric</th>
              <th scope="col">May</th>
              <th scope="col">June</th>
              <th scope="col">Change</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {results.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{r.metric}</th>
                <td>{r.before}</td>
                <td>{r.after}</td>
                <td class:list={{ highlight: r.highlight }}>{r.change}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Sales, units and ad spend in June</h3>
      <dl>
        <dt>Total monthly sales</dt>
        <dd>
          $44,593 <strong>+14.1%</strong>
        </dd>

        <dt>Units sold</dt>
        <dd>
          1,048 <strong>+13.9%</strong>
        </dd>

        <dt>Advertising spend</dt>
        <dd>−2.85%</dd>

        <dt>Rest of the catalog (excluding the two main ASINs)</dt>
        <dd>+13.6%</dd>
      </dl>

      <blockquote>
        <p>
          Organic sales grew <strong>+28.3%</strong> and ROAS improved — while spending <strong>less</strong> on ads.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
    </section>

    <section id="key-takeaways">
      <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A unified Amazon content strategy creates a more consistent customer journey.</li>
        <li>
          Research-driven visuals and messaging help communicate product benefits and address purchasing objections.
        </li>
        <li>Stronger organic performance can support sales growth without increasing advertising spend.</li>
        <li>
          Coordinated listing content, A+ Content, Brand Story, Storefront and video strengthen conversion across the
          Amazon customer journey.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</ArticleLayout>
